    "encoding_note": "AFDX uses the standard IEEE 802.3 line encoding of the underlying PHY (e.g. MLT-3 / 4B5B for 100BASE-TX). The AFDX-specific 'encoding' is structural: the VL ID embedded in the destination MAC, the 1-byte Sequence Number before the FCS, and the BAG-based traffic shaping — not a special line code."
